---
import {
  gaussianPairPotential,
  gaussianSelfEnergy,
} from '../../../data/part07/ewaldCoulombModel.mjs';

const width = 650;
const height = 300;
const left = 58;
const right = 620;
const top = 34;
const bottom = 250;
const maxDistance = 3;
const maxPotential = 3;
const defaultWidth = 0.35;
const defaultDistance = 0.6;
const xMap = (distance) => left + (right - left) * distance / maxDistance;
const yMap = (value) => bottom - Math.min(value, maxPotential) * (bottom - top) / maxPotential;
const samples = Array.from({ length: 241 }, (_, index) => {
  const distance = 0.015 + (maxDistance - 0.015) * index / 240;
  return {
    distance,
    point: 1 / distance,
    smeared: gaussianPairPotential({ distance, charge1: 1, charge2: 1, width: defaultWidth }),
  };
});
const pathFor = (key) => samples
  .map((point, index) => `${index === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'} ${xMap(point.distance).toFixed(2)} ${yMap(point[key]).toFixed(2)}`)
  .join(' ');
const pointPath = pathFor('point');
const smearedPath = pathFor('smeared');
const defaultValue = gaussianPairPotential({ distance: defaultDistance, charge1: 1, charge2: 1, width: defaultWidth });
const fallbackRows = [0, 0.5, 1].map((distance) => ({
  distance,
  point: distance === 0 ? null : 1 / distance,
  smeared: gaussianPairPotential({ distance, charge1: 1, charge2: 1, width: defaultWidth }),
}));
---

<figure class="chapter-visual gaussian-charge" data-gaussian-charge>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创交互模型：点电荷与 Gaussian 涂抹电荷</strong>
    <span lang="en">Original interactive model: point charges and Gaussian-smeared charges</span>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="chapter-visual__controls gaussian-charge__controls">
    <label>
      <span>Gaussian width σ | 电荷宽度</span>
      <input type="range" min="0.15" max="0.70" step="0.05" value={defaultWidth} data-gaussian-width />
      <output data-gaussian-width-output>{defaultWidth.toFixed(2)}</output>
    </label>
    <label>
      <span>probe separation R | 探测间距</span>
      <input type="range" min="0" max={maxDistance} step="0.05" value={defaultDistance} data-gaussian-distance />
      <output data-gaussian-distance-output>{defaultDistance.toFixed(2)}</output>
    </label>
  </div>

  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${width} ${height}`} role="img" aria-labelledby="gaussian-title gaussian-desc">
    <title id="gaussian-title">Interaction of point charges and equal Gaussian charge distributions</title>
    <desc id="gaussian-desc">
      The point-charge Coulomb potential diverges as one over separation. The interaction between equal normalized Gaussian charge clouds remains finite at zero separation and approaches one over separation at distances large compared with the Gaussian width. Keyboard-operable controls change the width and probe distance.
    </desc>
    <line x1={left} y1={bottom} x2={right} y2={bottom} class="plot-axis" />
    <line x1={left} y1={top} x2={left} y2={bottom} class="plot-axis" />
    <path d={pointPath} class="gaussian-charge__point" />
    <path d={smearedPath} class="plot-curve" data-gaussian-smeared-path />
    <line x1={xMap(defaultDistance)} y1={top} x2={xMap(defaultDistance)} y2={bottom} class="gaussian-charge__probe" data-gaussian-probe />
    <text x={right} y="280" text-anchor="end">R</text>
    <text x="18" y="48">interaction</text>
    <text x={right - 96} y="52" class="gaussian-charge__legend-point">1/R</text>
    <text x={right - 96} y="74" class="gaussian-charge__legend-smeared">erf[R/(2σ)]/R</text>
  </svg>

  <div class="chapter-visual__readout gaussian-charge__readout" aria-live="polite">
    <span>smeared interaction</span><strong data-gaussian-potential>{defaultValue.toFixed(6)}</strong>
    <span>point interaction</span><strong data-gaussian-point>{(1 / defaultDistance).toFixed(6)}</strong>
    <span>single-cloud self energy</span><strong data-gaussian-self>{gaussianSelfEnergy({ charge: 1, width: defaultWidth }).toFixed(6)}</strong>
    <span>R=0 finite limit</span><strong data-gaussian-zero>{gaussianPairPotential({ distance: 0, charge1: 1, charge2: 1, width: defaultWidth }).toFixed(6)}</strong>
  </div>

  <div class="gaussian-charge__fallback">
    <p><strong>无 JavaScript 参考表 | No-JavaScript reference table</strong></p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>R</th><th>point 1/R</th><th>Gaussian interaction</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {fallbackRows.map((row) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{row.distance.toFixed(2)}</td>
            <td>{row.point === null ? 'diverges' : row.point.toFixed(6)}</td>
            <td>{row.smeared.toFixed(6)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>模型：</strong>两个相同、归一化的三维 Gaussian charge clouds，标准差 <code>σ</code>、电荷均为 <code>+1</code>；pair interaction 为 <code>erf[R/(2σ)]/R</code>，single-cloud self energy 为 <code>1/(2√πσ)</code>。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Model:</strong> two identical normalized three-dimensional Gaussian charge clouds of standard deviation <code>σ</code> and charge <code>+1</code>; the pair interaction is <code>erf[R/(2σ)]/R</code> and the single-cloud self energy is <code>1/(2√πσ)</code>.</p>
    <p><strong>验收：</strong><code>R→0</code> 时 pair interaction 收敛到 <code>1/(√πσ)</code>；<code>R≫σ</code> 时恢复 <code>1/R</code>；减小 σ 提高 self energy。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Acceptance:</strong> as <code>R→0</code>, the pair interaction approaches <code>1/(√πσ)</code>; for <code>R≫σ</code> it recovers <code>1/R</code>; reducing σ raises the self energy.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>这是解析 Gaussian 模型。真实 pseudopotential compensation charge 可能非 Gaussian、带 angular components，并必须与 local potential 和 ionic self terms 一致。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> this is an analytic Gaussian model. A real pseudopotential compensation charge can be non-Gaussian, contain angular components, and must remain consistent with the local potential and ionic self terms.</p>
  </div>
</figure>

<script>
  import {
    gaussianPairPotential,
    gaussianSelfEnergy,
  } from '../../../data/part07/ewaldCoulombModel.mjs';

  document.querySelectorAll('[data-gaussian-charge]').forEach((root) => {
    const widthInput = root.querySelector('[data-gaussian-width]');
    const distanceInput = root.querySelector('[data-gaussian-distance]');
    const widthOutput = root.querySelector('[data-gaussian-width-output]');
    const distanceOutput = root.querySelector('[data-gaussian-distance-output]');
    const smearedOutput = root.querySelector('[data-gaussian-potential]');
    const pointOutput = root.querySelector('[data-gaussian-point]');
    const selfOutput = root.querySelector('[data-gaussian-self]');
    const zeroOutput = root.querySelector('[data-gaussian-zero]');
    const path = root.querySelector('[data-gaussian-smeared-path]');
    const probe = root.querySelector('[data-gaussian-probe]');
    if (!(widthInput instanceof HTMLInputElement) || !(distanceInput instanceof HTMLInputElement)) return;

    const left = 58;
    const right = 620;
    const top = 34;
    const bottom = 250;
    const maxDistance = 3;
    const maxPotential = 3;
    const xMap = (distance) => left + (right - left) * distance / maxDistance;
    const yMap = (value) => bottom - Math.min(value, maxPotential) * (bottom - top) / maxPotential;

    const update = () => {
      const width = Number(widthInput.value);
      const distance = Number(distanceInput.value);
      const curve = Array.from({ length: 241 }, (_, index) => {
        const sampleDistance = 0.015 + (maxDistance - 0.015) * index / 240;
        return {
          distance: sampleDistance,
          value: gaussianPairPotential({ distance: sampleDistance, charge1: 1, charge2: 1, width }),
        };
      }).map((point, index) => `${index === 0 ? 'M' : 'L'} ${xMap(point.distance).toFixed(2)} ${yMap(point.value).toFixed(2)}`).join(' ');
      if (path instanceof SVGPathElement) path.setAttribute('d', curve);
      if (probe instanceof SVGLineElement) {
        probe.setAttribute('x1', xMap(distance).toFixed(2));
        probe.setAttribute('x2', xMap(distance).toFixed(2));
      }
      if (widthOutput instanceof HTMLOutputElement) widthOutput.value = width.toFixed(2);
      if (distanceOutput instanceof HTMLOutputElement) distanceOutput.value = distance.toFixed(2);
      if (smearedOutput instanceof HTMLElement) smearedOutput.textContent = gaussianPairPotential({ distance, charge1: 1, charge2: 1, width }).toFixed(6);
      if (pointOutput instanceof HTMLElement) pointOutput.textContent = distance === 0 ? 'diverges' : (1 / distance).toFixed(6);
      if (selfOutput instanceof HTMLElement) selfOutput.textContent = gaussianSelfEnergy({ charge: 1, width }).toFixed(6);
      if (zeroOutput instanceof HTMLElement) zeroOutput.textContent = gaussianPairPotential({ distance: 0, charge1: 1, charge2: 1, width }).toFixed(6);
    };
    widthInput.addEventListener('input', update);
    distanceInput.addEventListener('input', update);
    update();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .gaussian-charge { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gaussian-charge svg { width: 100%; min-width: 38rem; }
  .gaussian-charge text { fill: currentColor; font-size: 13px; }
  .gaussian-charge__point { fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 2.1; stroke-dasharray: 7 4; }
  .gaussian-charge__probe { stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .gaussian-charge__legend-point { fill: currentColor; }
  .gaussian-charge__legend-smeared { fill: var(--sl-color-accent-high); }
  .gaussian-charge__controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .gaussian-charge__controls label { display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; }
  .gaussian-charge__readout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(10rem, 1fr)); gap: 0.4rem 1rem; }
  .gaussian-charge__fallback { max-width: 38rem; }
</style>
